{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/RS_TIMEX_00022","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/RS_TIMEX_00022@rel:R19-11#6161e503","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/RS_TIMEX_00022","release":"R19-11","content":"Support for Logical Execution Time Type: valid Description: The AUTOSAR templates shall provide the means to support the description of Logical Execution Time (LET) respectively Time Determinism. In particular the following shall be described: • Parameters of a LET interval : Length, type of recurrence and recurrence • The relation between LET intervals, like offset, gap and overlap. • Executable entities and/or groups of executable entities that shall be executed in the context of LET. • Data exchange that shall be conducted in the context of a LET interval, namely the time deterministic exchange of data between executable entities and/or groups of executable entities. • Means to specify an order of execution among a number of executable entities. Rationale: Time determinism is a crucial characteristic in embedded distributed real-time systems that ensures: • reliable operation of such systems due to deterministic data exchange and execution of executable entities, and • analysis and validation of such systems in order to perform timing analysis early in the development process. Use Case: Design and define timing behavior of applications as well as analysis and validation of timing behavior. Dependencies: [RS_TIMEX_00001], [RS_TIMEX_00002], [RS_TIMEX_00003], [RS_TIMEX_00004], [RS_TIMEX_00006] Supporting Material: None","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_RS_TimingExtensions.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:12+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"6161e5033463f3cf6591755ad2196af42432920eff271fee43bcb224ecfd69d4","removed":["5 22 of 34  AUTOSAR CONFIDENTIAL  Document ID 410: AUTOSAR_RS_TimingExtensions Requirements on Timing Extensions AUTOSAR CP R19-11 4"]},"text_key":"5146941e16c0"}],"li